---
---

<section id="metrics">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="metrics-header">
      <div>
        <div class="section-label">The numbers</div>
        <h2 class="section-h2 display">Admin work has a cost.<br>Most orgs just haven't counted it.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="metrics-live"><span class="metrics-live-dot"></span>Based on Capacity Reviews</div>
    </div>
    <div class="metrics-grid">
      <div class="metric-cell metric-cell--hero">
        <div class="metric-eyebrow">Of total staff hours</div>
        <div class="metric-value display">40%</div>
        <div class="metric-sublabel">never reaches a client</div>
        <div class="metric-bar-wrap">
          <div class="metric-bar-track"><div class="metric-bar-fill"></div></div>
          <div class="metric-bar-legend"><span>40% admin work</span><span>60% program delivery</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="metric-counter-stat">
          <div class="metric-counter-val">10 hrs / wk</div>
          <div class="metric-counter-lbl">reclaimed per workflow, on average</div>
        </div>
        <div class="metric-label">Your team isn't slow. The hours just aren't all going where they should.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="metric-cell">
        <div class="metric-value display">8–12 min</div>
        <div class="metric-label">That's all a Capacity Review takes. No prep, no pitch. A conversation about where your hours are going.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="metric-cell">
        <div class="metric-value display">24 hr</div>
        <div class="metric-label">Your Operations Assessment lands in your inbox. Written and specific. Yours to keep.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="metric-cell">
        <div class="metric-value display">3</div>
        <div class="metric-label">The average number of bottlenecks we find in a Capacity Review. Usually one surprises the ED.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="metric-cell">
        <div class="metric-value display">Week 1</div>
        <div class="metric-label">When your first workflow goes live, on average. Not months from now. Week one.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
